{"id": "e138e79a-3051-4040-9310-ec84515f27c7", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is a quick security review I can handle directly without any tools. Looking at the policy, the combination of `iam:PassRole` with wildcard resource and `lambda:CreateFunction` jumps out as a serious privilege escalation risk — it would let someone create a Lambda function with an arbitrary role attached, effectively assuming any permissions that role has.

The `lambda:InvokeFunction` and `s3:GetObject` with `Resource: "*"` compound the problem, granting unscoped access to invoke any function or read any object, far beyond what a build process should need. This is a bounded, answerable question I can address directly.

"}]}
